  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The JEDIEL project in Senegal, implemented by Social Change Factory is a civic engagement program designed to: &#x201c;awaken, strengthen, and amplify&#x201d; the voices of young Senegalese people around three major cross-cutting issues: democracy, gender, and climate justice. Over a period of four months, the project aims to raise awareness and engage young people and their communities through interactive training sessions, citizen debates, and a national advocacy competitio. &#xa0; The key activities intend to Equip young people with tools on the cross-cutting themes of gender, democracy, and climate justice through interactive modules in order to position them as agents of change</narrative>
  </description>
